WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.960
India issued 80 million free gas connections yet 90% of users still burned firewood. This is unintended consequences, episode 150, a health promise made in Baliya, a roll-out built for speed, the refill math that never covered a year of cooking, an audit of what left the kitchen and a metric that still cannot see the fire. On May 1, 2016 Prime Minister Narendra Modi stood in Baliya, in Uttar Pradesh and launched the Pradhan Mantri Ujwala Yojana.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:35.440
The promise was free-liquified petroleum gas connections, LPG, for 50 million poor households.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.780
Women would no longer have to cook over wood and dung.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.260
The problem the scheme was built to answer was not abstract.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.800
Indoor air pollution from solid fuels was estimated to cause hundreds of thousands of premature

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.800
deaths each year.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.780
Women and children took the hardest hit because the smoke lived in the room where the meal

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:54.300
was made.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:01:00.620
Moti's government, like earlier administrations, treated LPG as the practical, clean fuel already

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.180
sitting inside most districts.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.020
Cylinders were already moving to rural dealers.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.100
Distribution networks already reached most blocks.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.560
What looked missing was the first payment, not a new market and not a new forest policy.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.020
So the scheme aimed at that first barrier.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.320
The connection, the regulator, and the first cylinder.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.120
Cover up to 1,600 rupees.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:22.260
ities.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.000
Register the connection in an adult woman's name.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.160
Officials hope that ownership would become daily use, and that daily use would show up

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.340
as less smoke in the house.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.300
At the time, that chain looked straightforward, and it looked measurable.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.220
Earlier subsidy schemes had already taught a hard lesson about cash.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:43.980
Households rarely bought the opening hardware when money was thin at the start of a season.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:48.700
Paying for that first step was meant to clear the moment when a family was most likely to

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.260
walk away.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.700
Putting the asset in the woman's name was meant to give her leverage inside the household

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.360
budget when the next refill decision arrived.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.860
She would hold the papers.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.260
The next cylinder would, in theory, be hers to claim.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.240
That framing also fit how a government can run a large program.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.140
Numeric targets could be tracked through oil marketing company records.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.980
Nobody had to stand in a kitchen and count whether the fire that night was gas or wood.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.440
The connection itself was treated as the decisive intervention.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.680
A fortability of the first step stood in for a deeper change in fuel prices or in who

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.340
could still walk into a forest and come home with fuel that carried no bill.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.040
The people designing this were working a real death toll with a fuel the country already

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:31.860
knew how to move.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.940
The bet was that once the hardware crossed the threshold, the rest of the cooking year

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.540
would follow.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.740
Oil marketing companies built the rollout around Ujwala mellas.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.100
Applications moved through the socio-economic and caste census list.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:51.660
The target did not stay at 50 million. It rose to 80 million connections. Press releases

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.640
from the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas recorded the pace in public. 20 million

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:07.040
connections in 2016-17. 15.6 million in 2017-18. 36.2 million in 2018-19. By June 2019,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:13.820
the cumulative total stood at 72.3 million. Early coverage celebrated the speed. The government

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:17.140
Department described the program as a direct step toward smoke-free villages.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.520
The mellas made that claim visible.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:23.960
Local officials and company representatives could hand over the connection documents,

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.840
the stove, and the first cylinder in a single afternoon.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.400
A photograph could hold the whole achievement.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.700
A report could count at the same day.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.480
The administrative load per household stayed low enough for the oil companies to meet monthly

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.060
quotas.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.640
What the file needed was the woman's name and an address check.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.500
That same speed shaped what the file did not deeply test. Whether the household

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:51.160
already held an LPG connection somewhere else rested largely on ad-har matching. An audit

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:56.060
would later flag that step as incomplete. For a program judged on connections delivered,

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.980
incomplete matching was a cost of moving fast, not yet a crack in the story. Proponents could

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.320
point at villages receiving hardware that poor households had not been buying on their own.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.020
Skeptics, even then, would have had to ask a question the photographs could not answer.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:16.160
What happens on the afternoon after the mella when the first cylinder is empty and the next

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:16.860
one has a price?

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.820
The Comptroller and Auditor General later looked at what happened after the connection arrived.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:27.260
Among beneficiaries who had held a connection for more than a year, average annual refills

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.180
stood at 3.66 cylinders as of March 31, 2018.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:36.080
By December 31, 2018, that average had fallen to 3.21.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.500
A refill lasts roughly a month for a typical household.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:43.200
Three cylinders therefore covered only about three months of cooking.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.880
The other nine months had to be fueled somehow.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:52.780
A study of 4,994 households across 500 villages in the Central Indian Highlands landscape,

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:59.460
published in 2021 in Energy Research and Social Science, found LPG owning families still gathering

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:04.640
and burning firewood. Researchers called the pattern fuel stacking, households kept the

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:10.560
free connection, purchased LPG became a supplement, not a replacement. Three pressures held the

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:17.240
older fuel in daily rotation, refill costs, irregular cash income, and would nearby that carried a

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:23.360
price of zero. When a household's cash arrives in one or two harvest sales, several hundred rupees for

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.140
a cylinder in a lean month sits next to school fees and medical costs. Those bills do not wait for the

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:34.620
next crop. Wood that can be gathered in an afternoon has no cash price. On most days

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:39.340
the wood wins. The survey also showed that households with more forest within easy

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:44.320
walking distance were more likely to keep collecting every day, even after the LPG connection

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:50.200
arrived. The marginal cost of another trip remained zero. Distance to trees mattered as much

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.660
as the paper in the woman's name. That is a second order effect the connection count

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:59.660
could not see. The scheme had prioritized poor and forest fringe households because the

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:04.480
smoke burden was heaviest there. Those were also the places where free wood was closest,

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.660
and where cash was most seasonal. The groups named first for the hardware were the groups for

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:14.420
whom daily replacement was hardest. There was a partial gain, and it should be said plainly.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.400
Longer ownership correlated with fewer collection hours. For some families, total firewood volume

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.520
did fall. The drop was gradual. It never reached full displacement for the great majority.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:30.400
A connection could shave hours off a wood trip and still leave a wood fire as the ordinary

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.560
way to cook. Health gains that depend on the fire going out do not arrive on the same schedule

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:42.580
as a handover. The audit found another break in the chain. 198,000 beneficiaries averaged more than

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:48.820
12 cylinders a year. That volume is improbable for a domestic kitchen. It suggested some cylinders

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:53.900
were being diverted to commercial kitchens. Multiple daily refills at single bottle connections

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:59.940
pointed the same way. Some subsidized fuel left the domestic system entirely. That is a third

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:05.180
order effect. Cylinders diverted to commercial use are cylinders no longer available for the

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:10.120
household's the scheme named. Any simple count of health gains from connections delivered becomes

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:14.940
harder to read, because some of the subsidized fuel never stayed in the room where the smoke was

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:19.960
supposed to fall. None of this required bad faith at the launch in Bollyah. It required

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:25.778
a price, a season, and a forest that the connection record did not contain. The audit prompted

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:30.678
tighter checks on refill patterns. Emphasis shifted, at least in the language of review,

00:07:31.158 --> 00:07:36.418
toward sustained use rather than connection counts alone. Later government updates still reported

00:07:36.418 --> 00:07:41.678
cumulative connections past the original 80 million target. Independent surveys kept finding

00:07:41.678 --> 00:07:44.118
the same stacking in forest adjacent districts.

00:07:44.698 --> 00:07:47.098
No large-scale reversal took the hardware back.

00:07:47.678 --> 00:07:50.018
State programs began experimenting instead.

00:07:50.598 --> 00:07:55.278
Targeted subsidies for additional cylinders, community-level alternatives to firewood.

00:07:55.738 --> 00:07:57.338
The core design stayed as it was.

00:07:57.958 --> 00:08:01.078
Pay once for access, then charge a market price for the fuel.

00:08:01.678 --> 00:08:06.278
Follow-up surveys in the same Central Indian Highlands landscape kept recording the same

00:08:06.278 --> 00:08:06.598
split.

00:08:06.598 --> 00:08:11.938
The probability of daily LPG use stayed lowest among the poorest households, and the

00:08:11.938 --> 00:08:16.598
most forest adjacent households. Those were exactly the groups the scheme had put first

00:08:16.598 --> 00:08:20.938
in line for the initial connection. The fix did not undo the metric that had made the

00:08:20.938 --> 00:08:21.998
program look finished.

00:08:22.578 --> 00:08:27.978
Titer checks can catch a suspicious refill pattern. They do not, by themselves, put cash in a

00:08:27.978 --> 00:08:32.918
lean month, or put a price on an afternoon in the forest. Experiments with extra cylinder

00:08:32.918 --> 00:08:37.458
subsidies and community firewood alternatives were an admission that the second cylinder

00:08:37.458 --> 00:08:38.478
was the real test.

00:08:38.978 --> 00:08:43.198
They were also still small next to a national design that treated the first handover

00:08:43.198 --> 00:08:44.098
as the intervention.

00:08:44.738 --> 00:08:47.578
Where things stood after the audit was not a cancelled scheme.

00:08:48.178 --> 00:08:52.698
It was a scheme still adding names, besides surveys that still found wood and daily use,

00:08:53.218 --> 00:08:55.298
in the places the names had been meant to protect.

00:08:56.018 --> 00:09:01.078
A connection is hardware, a kitchen without wood smoke is a choice that has to win every afternoon

00:09:01.078 --> 00:09:03.718
against a fuel that costs time and nothing else.

00:09:04.531 --> 00:09:09.331
When success is the number of connections transferred, oil marketing company records can

00:09:09.331 --> 00:09:10.151
close the file.

00:09:10.751 --> 00:09:15.531
Months of cooking without fire would never enter that file, so the cheaper or free alternative

00:09:15.531 --> 00:09:16.451
stays in the pot.

00:09:17.271 --> 00:09:21.171
Registering ownership in a woman's name was meant to move the next refill decision.

00:09:21.691 --> 00:09:26.091
The refill costs still landed on a budget that rose and fell with agricultural seasons.

00:09:26.731 --> 00:09:28.831
The connection became an occasional convenience.

00:09:28.831 --> 00:09:33.371
science. When diversion controls are weak, some of the subsidized fuel leaves the domestic

00:09:33.371 --> 00:09:37.911
system, and the health arithmetic attached to the original list gets harder to trust.

00:09:38.831 --> 00:09:43.371
Environmental intelligence follows the smoke, the forest edge, and the rules that sit between

00:09:43.371 --> 00:09:48.691
them when a clean fuel promise meets a landscape that still supplies free wood. The same split

00:09:48.691 --> 00:09:53.691
is live in any clean fuel effort that scores itself on kits delivered. Induction sets

00:09:53.691 --> 00:09:58.911
counted at the warehouse, pellet stovs logged as distributed while the next bag of fuel waits on

00:09:58.911 --> 00:10:04.171
a harvest. Household Electric Connections celebrated before anyone asks whether the monthly bill

00:10:04.171 --> 00:10:09.271
can survive a lean season. If you were the person scoring one of those programs in month 12,

00:10:09.751 --> 00:10:14.731
what would you watch that a handover photograph cannot show? And that's where today's story leaves

00:10:14.731 --> 00:10:20.451
us. If it changed how you see one everyday decision, that's the whole point. Pass it along to someone

00:10:20.451 --> 00:10:23.391
who depreciate it, and we'll be back tomorrow with another case.

